<concept base="Top" id="t00164">
	<title id="e01198">Mechanical key</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>keys 
					<indexterm>mechanical key</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
				<indexterm>mechanical key</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<p>When the battery of the smart key is discharged or the smart key does not operate normally, the door can be locked or unlocked using the mechanical key.</p>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e01199">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e01200">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/N_CT25C002.eps" align="center" placement="break" id="e01201"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>To remove the mechanical key (2), pull the mechanical key protective cover (1) from the mechanical key.</p>
	</conbody>
</concept>